      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Mary's_City%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town's name honors Queen Henrietta Maria, with early settlers calling the area \"Terra Mariae.\".",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Mary's_City%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Today the site operates as an outdoor living‑history museum where costumed actors reenact colonial life and a replica of the Dove sails.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Mary's_City%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1969, Saint Marys City was declared a National Historic Landmark, recognizing its preserved colonial layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Mary's_City%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area hosts an internationally recognized archaeological research center and training field school for students worldwide.",
